{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The SanDisk SD card fits my repeated purchases of removable memory, card storage cases, and a card reader; I could use it as a spare for compatible camera equipment.",
    "The Fire TV Stick offers a useful next step for my television setup by adding streaming, and its TV controls give me a concrete reason to consider it."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "The large external drive and internal SSD share a storage theme with my memory cards, but neither fits my current need for small, removable media and practical accessories.",
    "My photography accessories do not imply an interest in a monitoring camera, and my device purchases do not create a current need for smart speakers, earbuds, or additional wired network connections."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My interest in electronics seems to have been treated as a reason to recommend many unrelated devices, even when they serve purposes I have not shown interest in.",
    "Owning a Fire tablet seems to have been taken as interest in Echo speakers, although I need a specific practical use before adding another device."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "I repeatedly choose accessories that support equipment I already use, such as memory cards, readers, mounts, cables, and lens caps; that practical connection matters to me.",
    "The kind of storage and its compatibility matter more than capacity alone: buying SD and microSD cards does not mean I need a 16TB drive or an internal computer upgrade."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations partly recognized my television and removable-memory needs but stretched my practical accessory purchases into interest in unrelated electronics."
}"}
